+# mutation — source-level mutant runner
+
+Runs curated source-level mutants against the test suite and reports
+`KILLED` (suite red) or `SURVIVED` (suite green) per mutant. A mutant that
+cannot be built or run reports `ERROR`, never a silent pass.
+
+## Usage
+
+```sh
+go run . [-persist-dir dir] [-test-tmpdir dir] [-dry-run] <repo> <mutants.json>
+```
+
+- `<repo>` — path to a graalgo checkout.
+- `<mutants.json>` — `{"mutants": [{"id", "lang": "java"|"go",
+  "file" (repo-relative), "old", "new", "description"}]}`. Every `file`
+  must exist in the repo and every `old` string must be present; the spec
+  is validated up front and rejected (exit 2) otherwise. A pattern
+  occurring more than once mutates the first occurrence only (with a
+  warning).
+- `-dry-run` — print the suite and mutant-build commands that would run,
+  plus prerequisite status, without running anything.
+- `-test-tmpdir dir` — directory for Java/Go temp files during suite runs.
+  Default is `<repo>/internal/backend/truffle/out/test-tmp`, the same
+  tmpdir discipline as the truffle Makefile. Override it when the repo
+  tree is read-only or quota-closed (e.g. `-test-tmpdir /tmp/mutation-tmp`).
+- `-persist-dir dir` — also write the report JSON into this directory
+  (created if needed). Empty (the default) means no persist: the report
+  lives in the temp workdir whose path is printed. There is deliberately
+  no default persist location — per-run evidence does not belong in the
+  repo (see the no-debris rule, graalgo `AGENTS.md` §5).
+
+Exit codes: 0 = run complete (see the `killed=/survived=/errors=` summary;
+an `ERROR` verdict is a tooling failure, not a kill), 1 = fatal (baseline
+not green, unwritable report, missing prerequisites), 2 = usage/spec error.
+
+## Prerequisites (checked before the baseline; fail fast)
+
+- Built backend class trees: `internal/backend/truffle/out/classes`,
+  `internal/backend/runtime/out/classes`, `internal/backend/truffle/out/test-classes`
+  including `graalgo/test/Runner.class`.
+  Build with `make -C internal/backend/truffle main` and
+  `make -C internal/backend/truffle out/test-classes/.built`.
+- Truffle jars in `internal/backend/truffle/lib/`.
+- A `gofrontend` binary: `GRAALGO_GOFRONTEND` when set, else
+  `<repo>/internal/frontend/gofrontend` (build with `./build.sh build`
+  in `internal/frontend/`).
+- Toolchain binaries: `GRAALGO_JAVA`/`GRAALGO_JAVA_RUN` (javac/java) and
+  `GRAALGO_GO` (go), defaulting to the pinned paths under `~/tools/`.
+
+## Mutant-runner contract
+
+- **Java mutants** (`lang: "java"`, file under
+  `internal/backend/<module>/src/main/java/...`) are compiled with
+  `javac -Xlint:deprecation -Werror` against the live class trees
+  (`runtime/out/classes : truffle/out/classes : truffle/lib/*.jar`) and
+  run with the overlay directory first in the test classpath. Only the
+  `truffle` module has a wired suite runner (`graalgo.test.Runner`); a
+  mutant in another backend module fails loudly with `ERROR` instead of
+  running the wrong suite. To wire another module, add a layout
+  constructor like `truffleLayout` plus its runner, and extend
+  `javaModuleFor` (see `main.go`).
+- **Go mutants** (`lang: "go"`, file under `internal/frontend/`) are built
+  with a Go overlay that merges `internal/frontend/build.sh`'s vendoring
+  map with one `Replace` entry for the mutated file, so the binary is
+  exactly `build.sh`'s binary plus one edit. The repo tree is never
+  modified. The suite then runs with `GRAALGO_GOFRONTEND` pointing at
+  the mutated binary.
+- **The suite** is `graalgo.test.Runner`, invoked exactly as
+  `internal/backend/truffle/Makefile`'s `test` target invokes it: same
+  runner class, same classpath order
+  (`[overlay :] out/test-classes : runtime/out/classes : out/classes : lib/*.jar`),
+  same `-Dgraalgo.repo.dir=<repo>` (the corpus tests resolve the corpus
+  through it), same `-Xss32m`, same tmpdir discipline
+  (`TMPDIR`/`GOTMPDIR`/`-Djava.io.tmpdir`). The baseline control runs the
+  clean tree first; a red baseline is fatal, so a mutant can never be
+  "killed" by a broken tree.
+- **Errors are never swallowed.** Report rendering, report writes,
+  persist writes, overlay compiles, log creation, and tmpdir creation
+  all return their errors; the run fails loudly instead of persisting an
+  empty report or reporting a verdict it did not measure.
+
+## Tests
+
+```sh
+go vet ./... && go test ./...
+```
+
+`main_test.go` pins the contract: no `phases/` or `hidden_files` in any
+constructed classpath, the shipped `mutants.json` resolves against the
+live tree, error paths return errors, the vendoring-overlay merge, and
+the suite command mirroring the Makefile. Tests that need the repo tree
+resolve it from the test file's location; when the module is staged
+outside the repo, set `MUTATION_TEST_REPO=<repo>`.
+
+## History
+
+Repointed 2026-11-07 (REVIEW-2026-11-07-07 R-05): the tool pointed at the
+deleted `phases/phase1` tree for its javac classpath, suite workdir, and
+report persistence, so every mutant errored and running it recreated
+`phases/phase1/hidden_files/` in the repo. The fix repoints the Java leg
+at `internal/backend/*`, the Go leg at the overlay build, moves
+persistence to opt-in, and checks every write.
